### Service request and approval demo (acceptance steps 3-7). Start the application first (see README),
### then run the requests in order. Uses the demo users seeded by DemoUserSeeder. No AI calls.

### 1. Login as employee
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "employee1", "password": "Employee#123"}

> {% client.global.set("employeeToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2. Login as supervisor
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "supervisor1", "password": "Supervisor#123"}

> {% client.global.set("supervisorToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 3. Employee creates a draft -> 201, status DRAFT
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": "CARD_SERVICE",
  "customerReference": "CUST-1001",
  "cardLastFour": "4821",
  "description": "Customer lost their debit card; block it and issue a replacement."
}

> {% client.global.set("requestId", response.body.id); %}

### 4. Invalid draft -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED (a card request needs the card's last 4 digits)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"category": "CARD_SERVICE", "description": "Replace card"}

### 5. Employee edits the draft (only while DRAFT) -> 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": "CARD_SERVICE",
  "customerReference": "CUST-1001",
  "cardLastFour": "4821",
  "description": "Customer lost their debit card at an ATM; block it and issue a replacement."
}

### 6. Employee submits -> 200, status PENDING_APPROVAL
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requests/{{requestId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 7. Employee tries to approve through the API -> 403 FORBIDDEN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 8. Employee lists their own requests
GET http://localhost:8080/api/requests/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 9. Supervisor sees the approval queue
GET http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 10. Executing before approval -> 409 CONFLICT
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/execute
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 11a. Supervisor approves -> 200, decision APPROVED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 11b. ...or rejects with a reason (instead of 11a, on a fresh pending request)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Customer reference does not match the ID shown"}

### 11c. ...or edits and approves (instead of 11a, on a fresh pending request)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/edit-and-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerReference": "CUST-2002"}

### 12. Supervisor runs the simulated execution -> 200, status EXECUTED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/execute
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 13. Executing again -> 409 CONFLICT (no duplicate execution)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/approvals/{{requestId}}/execute
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

### 14. The request with its full history (every field change and status move)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### 15. The audit trail of this request's decision and execution is in audit_events (SQL):
###     SELECT action, actor_id, details, correlation_id, created_at FROM audit_events
###     WHERE entity_type = 'SERVICE_REQUEST' ORDER BY created_at;
